            <ArticleTitle>Lupus anticoagulant and off-pump coronary bypass: dilemma of anticoagulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Confronted with a persistently elevated activated partial thromboplastin time due to circulating lupus anticoagulant in a patient undergoing emergency off-pump coronary artery bypass surgery, the dilemma of providing adequate anticoagulation for a short cardiac surgical procedure is highlighted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
